      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should seek emergency care immediately rather than trying to sleep it off; the combination of a head injury and blood thinner use (Eliglis for afib) significantly increases your risk of uncontrolled internal bleeding or delayed hematoma. Symptoms like a worsening headache, vomiting, confusion, or vision changes require urgent evaluation regardless of whether external bleeding occurs. Please do not wait until morning and contact your doctor or an emergency department right away for assessment.",
